   "text": "The drawing is a cyclodextrin with eight glucose units in the ring. Each unit carries a \u2013CH2\u2013S\u2013CH2CH2\u2013COOH group at C6, and I counted eight such sulfur chains. This matches the \u03b3-cyclodextrin derivative sugammadex, a per-6-deoxy-6-(2-carboxyethylthio) \u03b3-cyclodextrin.\n\nI wrote the SMILES largely from recall of the sugammadex structure rather than deriving each stereocentre from the wedges and hashes. I checked the connectivity (eight units, eight thioether acid chains) against the image. I did not verify the stereo descriptors centre by centre.\n\nSMILES: C(CSC[C@@H]1[C@@H]2[C@@H]([C@H]([C@H](O1)O[C@@H]3[C@H](O[C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H]3O)O)O[C@@H]4[C@H](O[C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H]4O)O)O[C@@H]5[C@H](O[C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H]5O)O)O[C@@H]6[C@H](O[C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H]6O)O)O[C@@H]7[C@H](O[C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H]7O)O)O[C@@H]8[C@H](O[C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H]8O)O)O[C@@H]9[C@H](O[C@H](O2)[C@@H]([C@H]9O)O)CSCCC(=O)O)CSCCC(=O)O)CSCCC(=O)O)CSCCC(=O)O)CSCCC(=O)O)CSCCC(=O)O)CSCCC(=O)O)O)O)C(=O)O"
